                <pb facs="0518" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg448"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">713.1311/279: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-03-07T14:00:00-06:00">March 7, 1934—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. My telegram No. 20, March 6, 6 p.m. Honduran Minister for Foreign Affairs now
                    tells me that Honduran Government now agrees with Nicaragua, Salvador, and
                    Guatemala to hold Conference on March 15 as originally planned, and that
                    Honduran delegates will be appointed tomorrow.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Central American missions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
